## 1. the original flip, as captured by T8

The failing run's raw log survived in the T8 scratch directory. Every one of
the twelve spatch invocations printed the same line and none of them analysed a
file (there is no HANDLING: line anywhere in the capture):

$ grep -n "Py.find\|Compilation OK" /tmp/sm750-static.mje5yt/coccinelle.log

# deref-under-null-check.cocci
...
$ grep -c 'HANDLING:' /tmp/sm750-static.mje5yt/coccinelle.log
0

The same run's gate summary (T8, /mega/tmp/sm750/t8/static.log):

coccinelle: exit 255, 0 finding(s)
  spatch failed, see /tmp/sm750-static.mje5yt/coccinelle.log
static gate: FAIL (raw logs in /tmp/sm750-static.mje5yt)

sparse, smatch, cppcheck and pahole exited 0 in that run, so the disagreement
was confined to spatch.

## 2. what the probe under test actually asks pkg-config

spatch's Python bridge is loaded for every .cocci that carries a
@script:python rule. At load time it locates libpython with
`pkg-config --libs python-3.14`. The wrappers in /mega/tmp/sm750/t24/shim
recorded the argv of every pkg-config call spatch made:

$ cat pkgconfig-calls.log        (PATH shim in front of /usr/bin/pkg-config)
ARGV: --libs python-3.14

/usr/lib64/pkgconfig/python-3.14.pc declares libdir=/usr/lib64 and
`Libs: -L${libdir}`, and pkg-config suppresses a -L for a system directory:

## probe 1: clean environment
$ env -u PKG_CONFIG_SYSROOT_DIR -u PKG_CONFIG_PATH pkg-config --libs python-3.14
$
[exit 0]

## probe 2: docs/ENVIRONMENT.md section 4 exported
$ PKG_CONFIG_PATH=/mega/tmp/sm750/t3/libdrm/usr/lib64/pkgconfig PKG_CONFIG_SYSROOT_DIR=/mega/tmp/sm750/t3/libdrm pkg-config --libs python-3.14
-L/mega/tmp/sm750/t3/libdrm/usr/lib64
[exit 0]

## probe 3: PKG_CONFIG_SYSROOT_DIR alone is sufficient
$ PKG_CONFIG_SYSROOT_DIR=/mega/tmp/sm750/t3/libdrm pkg-config --libs python-3.14
-L/mega/tmp/sm750/t3/libdrm/usr/lib64
[exit 0]

So the probe's answer is the empty string in a clean shell and a sysroot-
prefixed -L in a shell that carries docs/ENVIRONMENT.md section 4's variables.
PKG_CONFIG_SYSROOT_DIR alone is enough; PKG_CONFIG_PATH is not needed to
trigger it.

